# Slice 346 (the book, forms-declare-or-call): a place declared by the receiver of a reference is no Structure
# either. p refers to the Structure Model, which is no callable, so `p: other` neither applies anything nor declares:
# it is refused (8). Model itself can be declared again by `Model: other`; the reference is written by `p := Other`.
Model:
    int: v 1
end: Model
@: p Model
p: other
int: after Model\v
